# This directory is in a PUBLIC repository (alphastorm/dotfiles-ng).
#
# The corpus carries the answer key: every label, and `trap.ground_truth` plus
# `invalid_reason` for all twelve S4 traps. Publishing it would destroy the trap
# stratum outright -- the baits become searchable, and any model trained on public
# GitHub afterwards can recognize them -- and it would defeat the entire
# contamination apparatus in LRHE-PROTOCOL.md section 3.
#
# Corpus artifacts live in the private package instead:
#   ~/.dotfiles-private/omp-private/.omp/agent/skills/critical-review/lrhe-data/
#
# These patterns are a guard, not a policy. Do not remove them to "just commit the
# data"; move the data.
corpus.jsonl
packets.jsonl
sweep.jsonl
assignments.csv
findings.jsonl
judge*.jsonl
refute*.jsonl
exec.jsonl
human_queue.jsonl
canary*.jsonl
calibration*.csv
raw/
probes/
sim/
fixtures/
.cache/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.csv
report.json
analysis.json
# the real one is frozen next to the corpus in lrhe-data/
assignments.manifest.json
# provider terms snapshots are accumulated evidence, not replicable output:
# a later fetch returns a different document. They live beside the corpus.
terms/

# An unset variable in a documented command does not fail -- it makes a directory
# named for the variable. `$WORK/{runs,reviews}.jsonl` reached this public
# repository that way, and only `findings.jsonl` was caught, by name. Output
# addressed by a variable is never repository content.
$*
